<title>DENMARK: Singapore to raise Denmark, Norway air cargo rates.</title>
<headline>Singapore to raise Denmark, Norway air cargo rates.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore Airlines said on Tuesday it planned to raise freight rates from Denmark and Norway by five to seven percent from March 1.  </p>
<p>&quot;We are rasing rates from Denmark and Norway by five to seven percent as of March 1,&quot; Jens Heide, cargo manager Scandinavia and Finland for Singapore Airlines, told Reuters.</p>
<p>Heide said the carrier was not raising rates from Finland or Sweden, however.</p>
<p>&quot;The currencies have strengthened since we adjusted the rates last time,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>&quot;It's a local decision,&quot; he added.  </p>
<p>Copenhagen Airport is Singapore Airline's cargo hub in the Nordic region.</p>
<p>-- Abigail Schmelz, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969650</p>
</text>
